Title: F1-M07 — Black Glass (briefing)
Credit: Staalfront
Author: Staalfront narrative team
Draft date: 2026-10-17

FADE IN:

INT. COASTAL BUNKER - NIGHT

[[AMBIENCE: surf against concrete, wind in a gun slit, a map case snapping shut]]
[[MUSIC: low, restrained tension]]

A chart of the coast is spread across an ammunition crate. CAPTAIN ELIAN and MIRA stand over it.

MIRA
(serious)
Their sensor array has mapped our patrol routes for weeks. Every move we make is being anticipated.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(neutral)
Then we stop being anticipated.

[[SHOT: map]]
[[MAP: commando start in the south-west, drainage cut to the station walls, three masts inside, service road north, diversion force under trees in the north-west, signal ridge marker]]

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(measured)
A small team can cross the drainage cut unseen. The main force will draw their attention from the north.

MIRA
(firm)
Destroy the array and its backup generator. If either remains, the system will come back online.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(short)
Seven commandos. No base, no money, no replacements. The diversion goes in once, when your scout stands on the ridge marker.

MIRA
(dry)
A diversion that goes in before the culvert is open buys you nothing but a quieter funeral. Pick the moment.

CAPTAIN ELIAN
(pointing at map)
Sniper takes the culvert guards from range. Engineers follow. Charges on all three masts.

MIRA
(analytical)
The generator is not on the photographs, Captain. We know it exists because the array has never once gone dark. I cannot tell you where it is until the masts stop drawing power.

[[SFX: radio click]]
[[MUSIC: stop]]

FADE OUT.
